        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIGIbxca1V7_XU6X_uzDcYRa1quKvYZ0T1cuhnKYIo9J7J9ZQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "2 months ago",
        "text": "If could put 0 stars i would !\n⭐ 1 Star\nExtremely Dishonest, Unsafe, and Completely Unprofessional – Stay Away\n\nI’m writing this to warn anyone thinking of working with this company run by Wendy. My experience was absolutely terrible from beginning to end and became one of the worst business interactions I’ve ever had.\n\nI completed over $3,000 worth of work, and despite asking multiple times—over and over again—she never paid me the full amount owed. Every time I followed up, I got excuses, delays, or complete silence. At this point, it genuinely felt like she had no intention of paying from the start.\n\nWhat I witnessed on her job sites was even more alarming. In my personal experience, Wendy brought in workers who clearly did not have the required ASP cards, safety certifications, or legal permits to be working in construction. Several of these workers told me themselves that they were paid far below minimum wage, and some even mentioned they were not legally authorized to work in Canada.\nWhether or not that’s true, it raised massive red flags about how this company operates.\n\nThe entire operation felt careless, unsafe, and completely unprofessional. Between the non-payment, the avoidance, the questionable hiring practices, and the overall lack of integrity, I cannot stress enough how bad my experience was.\n\nIf you want to protect your money, your time, and your safety, stay far away from this company. I would never work with Wendy again, and I strongly advise others to avoid this business at all costs.\n\nAbsolutely NOT recommended.",
